# BDNSI global rule

- Existing mature Laravel system: audit and verify before modifying completed work.
- Current code, tests, CI and `.ai/PROJECT_STATE.md` outrank stale historical reports.
- MySQL 8.0 is canonical; do not switch authoritative testing to SQLite.
- Preserve RBAC, tenant isolation, financial invariants and document-access authorization.
- Never trust browser/client financial values or Center IDs.
- Never use destructive production DB commands or mutate legitimate production records for testing.
- Fix only verified gaps, retain/add meaningful tests, and prove every PASS with evidence.
- Routine safe engineering is autonomous; ask the owner only for destructive, credential-sensitive, production-data, or unresolved business-policy decisions.
- Never commit `.env`, private keys, or secrets. Use Cursor/environment secrets.
- Work on `cursor-development`; do not merge to `main` until release gates pass.
- Do not declare PRODUCTION READY until the latest verified code is deployed and independent live acceptance passes.